  "content": {
    "id": "p28-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "A bag contains five balls each labelled with a unique number from 1 to 5. Two balls are selected from the bag. Find the probability that the selection will contain numbers 1 and 2 if the balls are selected:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p28-q5-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "with replacement",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{2}{25}$",
          "worked": "The two possible orders are $(1,2)$ and $(2,1)$. Replacement leaves five balls available for the second draw.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{numbers 1 and 2})&=\\frac15\\times\\frac15+\\frac15\\times\\frac15\\\\P(\\text{numbers 1 and 2})&=\\frac{2}{25}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "without replacement.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{1}{10}$",
          "worked": "The two possible orders are $(1,2)$ and $(2,1)$. Without replacement, four balls remain for the second draw.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{numbers 1 and 2})&=\\frac15\\times\\frac14+\\frac15\\times\\frac14\\\\P(\\text{numbers 1 and 2})&=\\frac{1}{10}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      }
    ]
  },
